cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlowTwin, please cite it as below."
title: "FlowTwin: reinforcement-learning production scheduling on a digital twin of a packaging line"
authors:
  - family-names: Akremi
    given-names: Louay
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/louayakermi2816-gif/flowtwin"
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - reinforcement learning
  - production scheduling
  - discrete-event simulation
  - dispatching rules
abstract: >-
  A SimPy digital twin of a four-stage packaging line (filler, capper, labeller, packer)
  exposed as a Gymnasium environment. PPO and Double-DQN agents written from scratch in
  PyTorch are compared with dispatching rules on common seeded shifts under pre-registered
  protocols, and the twin is served live through FastAPI, MQTT and a Node-RED dashboard.
